# Line endings.
#
# Development happens on Windows (core.autocrlf=true), but production is the
# Linux image built from ./app/Dockerfile. Anything *executed inside that image*
# must keep LF endings: a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter
# named "/bin/bash -e\r" and the container dies with "bad interpreter". Pin those
# paths here so neither a Windows checkout nor a future commit can flip them.
app/bin/*         text eol=lf
app/Dockerfile*   text eol=lf
app/.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.sh              text eol=lf

# Loaded by psql inside the Linux container and contains dollar-quoted PL/pgSQL
# function bodies (the audit-log append-only trigger) — keep \r out of them.
app/db/structure.sql text eol=lf
